  "modelingNotes": [
    "The OSM outline and 14 m height locate the east museum wing. Twelve mapped roof plans lack heights, so the roof is kept low rather than giving them invented tall volumes.",
    "The museum describes two plain, perpendicular wings linked by an honor portico and Seine-facing terraces. This recipe emphasizes the long pale elevations, stepped parapet and open column rhythm visible in the exterior reference.",
    "Column intervals and roofline offsets are schematic. Sculpture, inscriptions and the adjoining Palais de Tokyo west wing are outside this asset."
  ],
